{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466502",
      "title": "Understanding the Core Module",
      "lectureOrder": 654,
      "videoOrder": 602,
      "sourceHash": "22dd98ad91cdff6ddfac6aad9862716979b01bd30212aaab50625b48706bbf8c",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 3.12,
          "en": "Instructor: Now that we had a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.12,
          "end": 5.79,
          "en": "at feature modules and shared modules,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.79,
          "end": 10.65,
          "en": "let's have a look at the third important module type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.65,
          "end": 11.97,
          "en": "you can work with,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.97,
          "end": 13.92,
          "en": "and that would be the CoreModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.92,
          "end": 16.92,
          "en": "And of course, let me highlight that all these modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.92,
          "end": 19.68,
          "en": "are created in the same way with NgModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.68,
          "end": 21,
          "en": "just the things we put in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21,
          "end": 22.8,
          "en": "and how we use them differs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.8,
          "end": 25.35,
          "en": "and that is what I mean with different module types.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.35,
          "end": 27.51,
          "en": "So what's the CoreModule?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.51,
          "end": 30.6,
          "en": "The CoreModule is basically there to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 30.6,
          "end": 33.18,
          "en": "make the AppModule a bit leaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 33.18,
          "end": 35.61,
          "en": "Let's say in the AppModule we have the AppComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 35.61,
          "end": 39.06,
          "en": "and here we are providing two services.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 39.06,
          "end": 41.31,
          "en": "Well then we can use a CoreModule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 41.31,
          "end": 44.01,
          "en": "to move these services out of the AppModule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.01,
          "end": 45.54,
          "en": "into the CoreModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 45.54,
          "end": 49.56,
          "en": "which then in turn, is added back to the AppModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 49.56,
          "end": 51.69,
          "en": "The alternative to that would of course be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 51.69,
          "end": 55.53,
          "en": "to use providedIn in @Injectable on the services,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55.53,
          "end": 58.47,
          "en": "which means we don't have to add them to providers at all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 58.47,
          "end": 61.26,
          "en": "But if you do add it to providers in the AppModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 61.26,
          "end": 63.9,
          "en": "well then using a CoreModule can be an idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 63.9,
          "end": 66.75,
          "en": "to again, keep your AppModule leaner.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 66.75,
          "end": 68.76,
          "en": "It's a pattern you see sometimes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 68.76,
          "end": 71.13,
          "en": "not a pattern you absolutely have to follow,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 71.13,
          "end": 72.09,
          "en": "and indeed, a pattern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 72.09,
          "end": 74.61,
          "en": "that you don't need to use or can't use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 74.61,
          "end": 77.76,
          "en": "if you are using providedIn in @Injectable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 77.76,
          "end": 79.98,
          "en": "which I will recommend using anyways.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 79.98,
          "end": 82.44,
          "en": "But if you do provide your services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 82.44,
          "end": 85.65,
          "en": "in providers of your AppModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 85.65,
          "end": 89.01,
          "en": "well then this is a pattern you might wanna use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 89.01,
          "end": 90.39,
          "en": "Let's have a look at that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 90.39,
          "end": 92.13,
          "en": "In our AppModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 92.13,
          "end": 93.84,
          "en": "if we have a look at the providers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 93.84,
          "end": 95.19800000000001,
          "en": "I have the ShoppingListService",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 95.19800000000001,
          "end": 96.33,
          "en": "and the RecipeService there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 96.33,
          "end": 98.07,
          "en": "and my interceptor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 98.07,
          "end": 101.1,
          "en": "Now, the idea behind the CoreModule is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 101.1,
          "end": 105.39,
          "en": "that we simply provide all these application-wide services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 105.39,
          "end": 108.57,
          "en": "that are important right from the start of the application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 108.57,
          "end": 110.72999999999999,
          "en": "that we provide them in a separate module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 110.72999999999999,
          "end": 113.31,
          "en": "which we then simply import into the AppModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 113.31,
          "end": 115.62,
          "en": "really just to keep this leaner",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 115.62,
          "end": 117.78,
          "en": "and to have a way or a place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 117.78,
          "end": 120.78,
          "en": "where we can quickly see all the core services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 120.78,
          "end": 122.25,
          "en": "of this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 122.25,
          "end": 123.6,
          "en": "Now, as I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 123.6,
          "end": 125.04,
          "en": "this does only make sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 125.04,
          "end": 127.32,
          "en": "or is only a pattern you may use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 127.32,
          "end": 129.39,
          "en": "if you are providing a service like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 129.39,
          "end": 132.24,
          "en": "by adding its type to the provider's array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 132.24,
          "end": 133.95,
          "en": "If you are providing a service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 133.95,
          "end": 135.93,
          "en": "like we're doing it for the data storage service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 135.93,
          "end": 138.54,
          "en": "where we pass this object to @Injectable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 138.54,
          "end": 140.25,
          "en": "where we set providedIn root,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 140.25,
          "end": 143.76,
          "en": "then this service is also provided application-wide,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 143.76,
          "end": 145.41,
          "en": "and you can't and shouldn't add it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 145.41,
          "end": 147.51,
          "en": "to providers of the AppModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 147.51,
          "end": 150.75,
          "en": "And this is indeed the approach I would recommend taking,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 150.75,
          "end": 153.78,
          "en": "I would not provide services in the AppModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 153.78,
          "end": 156.81,
          "en": "I would instead provide them application-wide, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 156.81,
          "end": 157.92000000000002,
          "en": "The effect's the same,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 157.92000000000002,
          "end": 161.85,
          "en": "but it keeps the AppModule cleaner and leaner automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 161.85,
          "end": 164.16,
          "en": "Still, for some things like the interceptors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 164.16,
          "end": 166.07999999999998,
          "en": "you have no alternative,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 166.07999999999998,
          "end": 168.21,
          "en": "you have to add them to providers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 168.21,
          "end": 169.82999999999998,
          "en": "And here for demo purposes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 169.82999999999998,
          "end": 173.19,
          "en": "I also added ShoppingListService and RecipeService.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 173.19,
          "end": 176.823,
          "en": "Then we can add a core.module.ts file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 177.87,
          "end": 179.613,
          "en": "where we export the CoreModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 180.6,
          "end": 182.85,
          "en": "And that again, is just a regular module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 182.85,
          "end": 185.673,
          "en": "with NgModule, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 186.69,
          "end": 189.9,
          "en": "An NgModule as before, now needs to be imported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 189.9,
          "end": 194.16,
          "en": "So NgModule from @angular/core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 194.16,
          "end": 198.66,
          "en": "Now here in NgModule, you add providers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 198.66,
          "end": 200.28,
          "en": "just providers array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 200.28,
          "end": 202.5,
          "en": "And there you simply add the providers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 202.5,
          "end": 205.623,
          "en": "you had in your AppModule, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 207.32999999999998,
          "end": 208.95,
          "en": "Now of course, for this to work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 208.95,
          "end": 211.35,
          "en": "you need to make sure you are importing all the things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 211.35,
          "end": 214.32,
          "en": "that you use in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 214.32,
          "end": 217.77,
          "en": "So I can grab these imports from the AppModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 217.77,
          "end": 220.88400000000001,
          "en": "we're in the end talking about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 220.88400000000001,
          "end": 222.65699999999998,
          "en": "the ShoppingListService, the RecipeService,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 222.65699999999998,
          "end": 224.67000000000002,
          "en": "and the AuthInterceptorService,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 224.67000000000002,
          "end": 226.53,
          "en": "I'll cut them from the AppModule",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 226.53,
          "end": 228.9,
          "en": "and move them here into the CoreModule.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 228.9,
          "end": 230.34,
          "en": "Import path is the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 230.34,
          "end": 232.35,
          "en": "because the CoreModule file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 232.35,
          "end": 234.93,
          "en": "is right next to the AppModule file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 234.93,
          "end": 237.54,
          "en": "And I also need the HTTP interceptors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 237.54,
          "end": 239.1,
          "en": "I can cut them from here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 239.1,
          "end": 240.873,
          "en": "And instead, you stay here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 242.19,
          "end": 244.2,
          "en": "add here to the CoreModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 244.2,
          "end": 246.15,
          "en": "import HTTP interceptors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 246.15,
          "end": 247.83,
          "en": "from @angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 247.83,
          "end": 251.133,
          "en": "Whoops, angular/common/http.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 253.05,
          "end": 256.44,
          "en": "So now the CoreModule here is prepared,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 256.44,
          "end": 259.29,
          "en": "you don't need to export your services",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 259.29,
          "end": 262.2,
          "en": "because services work differently than declarations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 262.2,
          "end": 264.36,
          "en": "Only declarations and other modules",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 264.36,
          "end": 265.74,
          "en": "need to be exported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 265.74,
          "end": 270.57,
          "en": "Services are automatically injected on a root level,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 270.57,
          "end": 273.3,
          "en": "you don't need to export them to make this happen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 273.3,
          "end": 275.88,
          "en": "So services are simply an exception.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 275.88,
          "end": 277.8,
          "en": "And therefore now in the AppModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 277.8,
          "end": 279.75,
          "en": "the only thing we have to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 279.75,
          "end": 284.75,
          "en": "is we have to import our CoreModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 285.81,
          "end": 287.34000000000003,
          "en": "even though it's not exporting anything,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 287.34000000000003,
          "end": 290.853,
          "en": "but to still include it here into our build process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 291.69,
          "end": 296.69,
          "en": "and we import it from our core.module file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 299.55,
          "end": 303.51,
          "en": "With that set up, the application restarts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 303.51,
          "end": 307.5,
          "en": "and you should still have the same functionality as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 307.5,
          "end": 310.86,
          "en": "I can fetch my recipes here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 310.86,
          "end": 312.87,
          "en": "Let's try deleting a recipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 312.87,
          "end": 315.51,
          "en": "which will use the recipe service behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 315.51,
          "end": 319.92,
          "en": "Let's test something here for my shopping list.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 319.92,
          "end": 321.84,
          "en": "This all still works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 321.84,
          "end": 324.51,
          "en": "so all these services still work,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 324.51,
          "end": 326.43,
          "en": "but now we have them in the CoreModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 326.43,
          "end": 328.02,
          "en": "which is our go-to place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 328.02,
          "end": 331.44,
          "en": "to quickly see our root application services,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 331.44,
          "end": 333.54,
          "en": "and we have a leaner AppModule,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 333.54,
          "end": 334.89,
          "en": "without a provider's array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 334.89,
          "end": 337.26,
          "en": "But as I mentioned, A, this is optional,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 337.26,
          "end": 338.97,
          "en": "and B, this is only required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 338.97,
          "end": 340.47,
          "en": "if you provide a service here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 340.47,
          "end": 343.56,
          "en": "instead of providing it through @Injectable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 343.56,
          "end": 346.533,
          "en": "which would be my recommendation to use whenever possible.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
